Parity projector channel atlas
Core rule: for an involution J, (f+fJ)/2 keeps invariant channels and (f-fJ)/2 keeps anti-invariant channels.
On a Boolean edge cube, global reversal x -> -x makes invariant functions even-Walsh and anti-invariant functions odd-Walsh.

1. Scalar midpoint gate
-----------------------
For a paired offset z around midpoint c:
degree 0: pair-sum z-powers [0]; pair-difference z-powers []
degree 1: pair-sum z-powers [0]; pair-difference z-powers [1]
degree 2: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2]; pair-difference z-powers [1]
degree 3: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2]; pair-difference z-powers [1, 3]
degree 4: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2, 4]; pair-difference z-powers [1, 3]
degree 5: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2, 4]; pair-difference z-powers [1, 3, 5]
degree 6: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2, 4, 6]; pair-difference z-powers [1, 3, 5]
degree 7: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2, 4, 6]; pair-difference z-powers [1, 3, 5, 7]
degree 8: pair-sum z-powers [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]; pair-difference z-powers [1, 3, 5, 7]
Faulhaber anchor warning: the prompt's interval balance is paired offsets plus one fixed center term c^p.
Thus the surviving scalar data are odd moment channels plus a fixed-point scalar atom.

